includes: The AUv3 hosting pillar starts here. Tools ▸ Plugins now lists the Audio Unit instruments and effects installed on your device — split into Instruments and Effects, de-duplicated and sorted — so you can see exactly what Echoel will be able to host in a channel. This is the safe, read-only first slice: it scans and shows, it doesn't yet load a plugin into the graph. Loading a chosen AUv3 into an Echoel channel (its sound in your audio graph, its own UI in an Echoel-framed panel, state saved/recalled) is the next step in this arc. Built on AVAudioUnitComponentManager with a pure, tested split/de-dupe/sort. Verified: Xcode Compile Check + CI green.
